this is sasha johnson a prominent  anti-racism campaigner she's fighting  for her life in hospital after  reportedly being shot in the head  the incident happened in southwark in  southeast london  police were called to an address on  consort road behind me at just after  three o'clock in the morning on sunday  it is there they say they found a 27  year old woman who had suffered from a  gunshot wound  detectives from the metropolitan  police's specialist crime command are  leading the investigation  in a statement the met says while the  investigation is at an early stage  there is nothing to suggest the woman  who was shot was the subject of a  targeted attack  or that she had received any credible  threats against her prior to this  incident  last august sasha johnson organised  large-scale march  to protest against systemic racism she  told sky news what drives her activism  the uk disassociates from racism but we  have to remember  the wind rush generation came here when  we're funding water bomb other countries  and people are coming here for safety  and rest  then we're flewing them away with our  xenophobia so we're not disassociating  from we're saying yes is here  we need to address it now we're in 2020.  we've come too far  for racism to still be a problem the 27  year old mother is a committee member of  the political party  taking the initiative the party says  it is with great sadness that we inform  you that our own sasha johnson  has sustained a gunshot wound to her  head  sasha has always been actively fighting  for black people  and the injustices that surround the  black community  so far there have been no arrests police  are appealing to anyone with any  information to come forward  jemima walker sky news
 

